# Registry configuration for deployment to Posit Connect.
#
# Connect runs `npm ci --omit=dev` inside the deployed bundle, so it reads this
# file. Without it, npm defaults to registry.npmjs.org, which the Connect build
# container cannot reach -- the install stalls for ~70s and npm then dies with
# "Exit handler never called!".
#
# The token is deliberately NOT stored here. npm expands ${NPM_TOKEN} from the
# environment, so this file is safe to commit and safe to ship in a bundle.
#
# IMPORTANT -- the ${NPM_TOKEN} line likely does NOT work on Connect yet.
# Connect's docs state that content environment variables are "decrypted only
# when a process is about to be started", i.e. at runtime, not during the
# package restore that runs `npm ci`. So a variable set via `rsconnect -E` or
# the content Vars panel probably expands to an empty string here, producing
# E401 rather than a successful install.
#
# The credential is documented as belonging on the SERVER, placed by a Connect
# administrator in one of:
#
#   /etc/npmrc                                (all users on the system)
#   ~/.npmrc for the Applications.RunAs user  (typically rstudio-connect)
#
# Bundle-level .npmrc settings like the registry line below still override
# server-level ones, so this file remains the right place for the registry.
# Only the auth token needs to come from the server.
#
# See: https://docs.posit.co/connect/admin/nodejs/package-management/
#
registry=https://artifactory.worldbank.org/artifactory/api/npm/itsdt-npm-virtual/
//artifactory.worldbank.org/artifactory/api/npm/itsdt-npm-virtual/:_authToken=${NPM_TOKEN}
